    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A traditional cottage located on the outskirts of Ballybofey town, occupying a large plot and very conveniently situated. Close to Sessiaghoneill Church and National School. Requiring renovation, this cottage has been vacant for a number of years and should qualify for both the 70,000 derelict home grant plus S.E.A.I. Energy Upgrade grants, subject to end user intentions. Internally fire damaged a few years ago, the cottage structurally suffered very little damage. Presently laid out with sitting room, kitchen, two small bedrooms plus bathroom on the ground floor plus two upstairs bedrooms in the attic space. Sure to generate lots of interest so early viewing is strongly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "<br><br>\nSitting Room - 3.3m x 3.3m <br>Open fireplace. \nFront facing window. \n9ft high ceiling.\nTongue and groove timber board ceiling. <br><br><br>\nKitchen - 3.8m x 3.3m <br>Solid fuel range. \nFront facing window. \nFront door. \nTiled floor.\n9ft ceiling height. \nTongue and groove timber board ceiling. <br><br><br>\nDownstairs Bedroom One - 2.4m x 2m <br>Rear facing window. <br><br><br>\nDownstairs Bedroom Two - 2.4m x 2m <br>Gable window. <br><br><br>\nBathroom - 2.8m x 2m <br>WC, WHB and bath. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Three - 5.5m x 3.9m Max. Measurement <br>Tongue and groove timber board pitched ceiling. \nGable window. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Four - 5.5m x 3.3m Max. Measurement <br>Tongue and groove timber board pitched ceiling. \nGable window. <br><br>"
